{"comparisons":[],"failures":[],"frontier":[],"initial":{"alternatives":{"coverage":[{"reason":"States the selected compulsory route, extended parallel period and commencement date.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u1"},{"reason":"Background heading; creates no separate duty.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u2"},{"reason":"Identifies the earlier circular, launch date, portal and application/submission context.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u3"},{"reason":"Explains parallel running and acceptance through existing channels.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u4"},{"reason":"Section heading linking extension and enhancements.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u5"},{"reason":"Describes monitoring and feedback; does not condition the compulsory route.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u6"},{"reason":"Extends parallel running through 29 November 2024 and explains its purpose.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u7"},{"reason":"Full-adoption heading supports the transition context.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u8"},{"reason":"Restates the compulsory route, describes integration of reporting requests and distinguishes optional fee settlement.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u9"},{"reason":"Enquiries heading; creates no submission requirement.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u10"},{"reason":"Practicability qualifies SFC operational enhancements; contact guidance creates no exception to the route.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u11"},{"reason":"Identifies issuing division.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u12"},{"reason":"Identifies issuing institution.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u13"},{"reason":"End marker has no substantive effect.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u14"},{"reason":"Identifies product categories associated with the IPD scope reference.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u17"},{"reason":"Expands WINGS; does not broaden the selected control.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u18"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The route applies to persons making applications or submissions concerning IPD-administered investment products. It is transaction-specific, with no bank-only actor limitation. The footnote identifies relevant product categories.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u9","u17"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"e-IP is the investment-product online application/submission system on WINGS. WINGS is expanded in footnote 2. The packet does not provide a complete test for classifying borderline communications as submissions or establish whether footnote 1 is an exhaustive taxonomy.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u9","u17","u18"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"Existing-channel acceptance belongs to the parallel period, extended through 29 November. No post-transition exception is stated. 'where practicable' attaches to SFC review and enhancement, not submission duties; optional fee settlement is a separate facility.","source_unit_ids":["u4","u7","u9","u11"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"'must' imposes the selected submission-route requirement. 'can also' offers fee settlement. Statements about future integration and enhancements do not impose separate user duties or make commencement conditional on technical completion.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u7","u9","u11"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The original 29 October endpoint is replaced by 29 November 2024; compulsory routing starts on 30 November 2024 inclusively. The text does not resolve attempted-versus-completed submission timing or expressly explain treatment of pending cases.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u4","u7","u9"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The 8 July 2024 launch circular and existing IPD submission requests supply referenced background whose full terms are absent. Dependency external-authorities.24ec50 has no supplied text or hash. These cannot establish additional exceptions, deadlines or filing duties.","source_unit_ids":["u3","u9"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Does the referenced launch circular specify how pending applications, supplementary documents and submissions attempted before but completed after 30 November 2024 are handled?","Is footnote 1 an exhaustive restriction on product scope, or an identification of the products then administered by IPD?","What determines the operative submission date, and which borderline communications qualify as submissions?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["Evaluate one application or submission event, not an institution's overall compliance.","The extended parallel period retains the existing-channel acceptance described for parallel running.","The operative submission date and product classification must be supplied from evidence; unknown values remain unknown."],"citations":[{"quote":"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.","unit_id":"u4"},{"quote":"To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.","unit_id":"u7"},{"quote":"Starting 30 November 2024, ie, after the parallel run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"The SFC will continue to review and enhance the operation of e-IP where practicable.","unit_id":"u11"},{"quote":"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.","unit_id":"u17"}],"distinction":"The strongest supported reading uses the date of each submission event. For example, an in-scope supplementary submission made on 2 December for an application initially lodged on 28 November falls within the route requirement. A case-opening-date approach would exempt it, but this packet provides no affirmative support for that grandfathering rule, so it is an unresolved question rather than a second proposed reading. An ordinary existing-channel submission on 29 November remains within parallel running; the same event on 30 November engages the compulsory route. Optional annual-fee settlement does not independently engage this control.","family":"time","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The evaluated event is an application or submission concerning an investment product administered by IPD, assessed with the product categories in footnote 1. Optional fee payment alone does not establish this classification.","name":"is_ipd_product_application_or_submission","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u9","u17"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean classification of the evaluated event"},{"meaning":"The operative date on which the evaluated application or submission is made. The packet does not determine this date for incomplete or disputed transmission events.","name":"submission_date","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"The evaluated application or submission is submitted to IPD through e-IP.","name":"submitted_via_e_ip","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean route fact for the evaluated event"}],"result":"submitted_via_e_ip","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_ipd_product_application_or_submission (>= submission_date (date 2024-11-30)))"},"local_id":"r1","questions":["Does omitted transition guidance expressly preserve existing channels for subsequent submissions on already-open cases?","For disputed transmission events, does submission occur on sending, receipt, acceptance or completion?"],"statement":"Selected control: compulsory e-IP submission route from 30 November 2024. Each in-scope application or submission made on or after that date must use e-IP. Existing-channel acceptance continues during the extended parallel period through 29 November. Neither planned enhancements nor the practicability qualification creates a stated exception. The result tests only route satisfaction within scope; it does not determine whether a filing is required, timely or substantively adequate.","subject":"Route for an individual IPD investment-product application or submission"}]},"controlled-language":{"coverage":[{"reason":"States the extended parallel period and compulsory route from 30 November 2024.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u1"},{"reason":"Background heading; no separate duty.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u2"},{"reason":"Identifies the earlier circular, launch date and new-product and post-authorisation/registration context; the earlier circular is not supplied.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u3"},{"reason":"Establishes existing-channel acceptance during the parallel run, whose endpoint is extended by u1 and u7.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u4"},{"reason":"Section heading; no separate duty.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u5"},{"reason":"Describes monitoring and feedback, without qualifying the submission obligation.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u6"},{"reason":"Extends the parallel run through 29 November 2024; enhancements explain the extension rather than condition the transition.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u7"},{"reason":"Full-adoption heading supports the transition context.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u8"},{"reason":"Restates the compulsory route, identifies integration of existing reporting requests, and separately permits annual-fee payment through e-IP.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u9"},{"reason":"Enquiries heading; no separate submission condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u10"},{"reason":"Practicability qualifies SFC operational improvements; the contact invitation does not create a submission exemption.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u11"},{"reason":"Identifies the issuing division.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u12"},{"reason":"Identifies the issuing commission.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u13"},{"reason":"Closing marker; no operative condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u14"},{"reason":"Supplies product categories attached to the IPD product scope.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u17"},{"reason":"Expands WINGS; does not prescribe an additional submission route.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u18"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The control concerns persons making applications or submissions to IPD for investment products administered by IPD. It does not establish a duty for every industry participant to make a filing. Existing reporting requests are included in the migration context.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u9","u17"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Footnote 1 supplies the product categories; e-IP is the online application/submission system and WINGS is its portal. The packet does not expressly settle whether the footnote is exhaustive or define every communication that counts as a submission.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u9","u17","u18"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"Existing-channel acceptance attaches to the parallel period. No post-transition exemption appears. 'Where practicable' attaches to SFC review and enhancement, not submitters' use of e-IP.","source_unit_ids":["u4","u7","u9","u11"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"'Must' makes the submission route compulsory. Integration and enhancements are announced system changes. 'Can also' makes annual-fee settlement through the system an optional facility.","source_unit_ids":["u7","u9","u11"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The extension replaces the original 29 October 2024 endpoint with 29 November 2024; compulsory routing begins on 30 November 2024. The text supplies no separate grandfathering rule for later filings concerning previously opened cases.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u4","u7","u9"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The 8 July 2024 circular and current IPD reporting requests are referenced but not supplied. Dependency external-authorities.24ec50 has no supplied text or hash. These materials could clarify classification and operating details; the stated transition is not expressly conditional on enhancement completion.","source_unit_ids":["u3","u7","u9"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Does footnote 1 exhaust the covered product categories, or describe the products currently administered by IPD?","What do the referenced 8 July 2024 circular and current IPD requests specify about submission classification, pending cases and the event that determines a filing's date?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["The unit of assessment is one application or submission event, not an institution's overall compliance.","Extending the parallel run carries forward the existing-channel acceptance described for that run.","The operative date is the date of the application or submission event; the packet supplies no separate initiation-date test.","Product and filing classification remain supplied facts requiring judgment where the packet does not resolve them."],"citations":[{"quote":"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.","unit_id":"u4"},{"quote":"To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.","unit_id":"u7"},{"quote":"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"The SFC will continue to review and enhance the operation of e-IP where practicable.","unit_id":"u11"},{"quote":"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.","unit_id":"u17"},{"quote":"Following the “Circular on launch of e-IP application/submission system on WINGS” dated 8 July 2024","unit_id":"u3"}],"distinction":"This reading applies the transition to each covered filing made from the stated date, including filings concerning existing products or cases where they qualify as submissions. It preserves the separate permission to pay annual fees through e-IP. A competing rule limited to cases initiated after the transition, or conditioned on completed enhancements, lacks sufficient textual support. The strongest uncertainty is the boundary of covered submissions and the treatment of pending-case events under the unavailable referenced materials.","family":"time","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed event is an application or submission to IPD concerning an investment product administered by IPD, taking account of footnote 1 and the reporting requests described in u9. Mere use of the optional annual-fee payment facility does not itself establish this classification.","name":"covered_filing","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u9","u17"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean classification of one filing event"},{"meaning":"Gregorian date on which the assessed application or submission is made. Determining the relevant event for attempted, incomplete or pending filings may require judgment.","name":"filing_date","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"Whether the assessed application or submission was submitted to IPD via e-IP, as established by the filing record.","name":"submitted_via_eip","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean route observation"}],"result":"submitted_via_eip","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and covered_filing (>= filing_date (date 2024-11-30)))"},"local_id":"route_transition_1","questions":["For an incomplete filing or a supplement to an existing case, which event determines the submission date?","Do the unavailable referenced materials specify any transition treatment that changes classification of pending-case filings?"],"statement":"Selected control—compulsory e-IP submission route: if a person makes an application or submission to IPD concerning an investment product administered by IPD on or after 30 November 2024, that filing must be submitted via e-IP. Existing channels remain accepted during the extended parallel run through 29 November 2024. The control specifies the route for covered filings; it does not independently create filing obligations, reporting frequencies or a compulsory e-IP route for annual-fee payments. Within the formal scope, a true result means this route condition is met and a false result means it is unmet; outside scope, no route-compliance conclusion is drawn.","subject":"Route used for an individual IPD investment-product application or submission"}]},"normative":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Establishes the circular’s subject and the compulsory e-IP route and transition date.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u1"},{"reason":"Section heading providing background context.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u2"},{"reason":"Describes launch history and purpose; supports dependency and chronology.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u3"},{"reason":"States the initial parallel-run arrangement and continued acceptance through existing channels.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u4"},{"reason":"Section heading for extension and enhancements.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u5"},{"reason":"Describes monitoring and industry feedback; contextual rationale for extension.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u6"},{"reason":"States enhancements and extension to 29 November 2024; supports transition timing.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u7"},{"reason":"Section heading for full adoption.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u8"},{"reason":"States the compulsory route from 30 November 2024 and identifies integrated submission requests and optional fee settlement.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u9"},{"reason":"Section heading for feedback and enquiries.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u10"},{"reason":"States continuing review and provides contact direction; no additional submission duty.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u11"},{"reason":"Identifies the Investment Products Division abbreviation’s referent.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u12"},{"reason":"Identifies the Securities and Futures Commission abbreviation’s referent.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u13"},{"reason":"Document terminator with no substantive rule.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u14"},{"reason":"Defines the footnote’s investment-product categories covered by “investment products.”","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u17"},{"reason":"Defines WINGS as Web-based INteGrated Service, a dependency for the launch description.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u18"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The mandatory route applies to applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD; footnote 1 supplies the listed product categories. The source does not state that optional recurring-fee settlement is compulsory.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u9","u12","u17"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"IPD means Investment Products Division; SFC means Securities and Futures Commission; WINGS means Web-based INteGrated Service; “investment products” is expanded by footnote 1.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u12","u13","u17","u18"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"During the parallel run, existing channels remain accepted. The text does not expressly preserve an exception after 30 November 2024, and recurring annual-fee settlement is described as an available capability rather than part of the compulsory route.","source_unit_ids":["u4","u9"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"“must be submitted via e-IP” creates a compulsory submission duty from 30 November 2024; “can also settle” describes permission or capability for recurring annual fees.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The initial parallel run ended 29 October 2024, was extended to 29 November 2024, and compulsory e-IP submission starts 30 November 2024. Launch occurred 29 July 2024.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u4","u7","u9"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The route depends on the product being administered by IPD and on the e-IP system on the SFC’s WINGS portal; the source also references integration of prior IP E-submission requests.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u9","u12","u18"],"status":"PROPOSED"}],"questions":["Does “applications and submissions” include every filing listed in the integrated IP E-submission requests, or are any categories governed by separate instructions?","After 30 November 2024, are existing channels unavailable in all cases, or can IPD authorize an exception?","Is recurring annual-fee settlement merely an optional facility, or is it mandatory for specified products under another instrument?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["“Investment products administered by IPD” is limited to products within the categories listed in footnote 1.","The transition date is interpreted by calendar date in Hong Kong without an unstated time-of-day rule.","The phrase “can also settle” is permissive and does not expand the compulsory submission duty."],"citations":[{"quote":"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.","unit_id":"u4"},{"quote":"Starting 30 November 2024, ie, after the parallel run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.","unit_id":"u9"}],"distinction":"Primary reading: the parallel run ends at the close of 29 November 2024, and from 30 November 2024 every covered IPD application or submission must use e-IP. Existing channels are accepted only during the parallel run. Recurring annual-fee settlement is an additional available function, not itself a compulsory filing route.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The selected filing is an application or submission of an investment product administered by IPD.","name":"covered_ipd_filing","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9","u17"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The filing date is on or after the compulsory transition date.","name":"filing_on_or_after_2024_11_30","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The covered filing was submitted through e-IP.","name":"submitted_via_e_ip","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(if (and covered_ipd_filing filing_on_or_after_2024_11_30) submitted_via_e_ip false)","result_type":"bool","scope":"Selected control: compulsory e-IP submission route for covered IPD applications and submissions."},"local_id":"r1","questions":["The source does not specify whether a filing initiated before 30 November but completed afterward is governed by the new route."],"statement":"From 30 November 2024, covered IPD applications and submissions must use e-IP; existing channels are accepted during the parallel run ending 29 November 2024.","subject":"Compulsory e-IP submission route"},{"assumptions":["“After the extended period” is read as beginning immediately after 29 November 2024.","The word “must” applies to applications and submissions, while the listed integrated requests clarify examples rather than limit the duty.","The source does not expressly state whether any legacy channel remains available by IPD discretion."],"citations":[{"quote":"To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.","unit_id":"u7"},{"quote":"Starting 30 November 2024, ie, after the parallel run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.","unit_id":"u9"}],"distinction":"Alternative reading: the duty is compulsory for the specified IPD submission requests, including the examples integrated from the IP E-submission system, but the text leaves open whether other communications or exceptional filings may continue through another channel with IPD approval. This reading treats the integration sentence as potentially delimiting the operational set rather than merely illustrating it.","family":"exceptions","formalization":null,"local_id":"r2","questions":["Does the integration sentence enumerate all compulsory submission types or only examples?","Does IPD retain authority to accept a legacy-channel filing after 30 November 2024?","Are recurring annual fees outside the selected compulsory control unless another rule applies?"],"statement":"The compulsory e-IP duty clearly begins on 30 November 2024, but the complete set of covered submission types and any post-transition exceptions are unresolved.","subject":"Extent of post-transition compulsory route"}]}},"java_checks":[],"live_provider":true,"model_calls":3,"no_progress":0,"nodes":[{"bundle_hash":null,"candidate_id":"candidate.b671443076f445349a4226565d2fa216","commitment":"5a422d7d232302a2e277a46f989d9f8172ff49fb7873b4381707356db61d4502","depth":0,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":{"code":"E_SCHEMA","details":"Invalid expression atom"},"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.5a422d7d232302a2e277a46f","order":0,"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["“Investment products administered by IPD” is limited to products within the categories listed in footnote 1.","The transition date is interpreted by calendar date in Hong Kong without an unstated time-of-day rule.","The phrase “can also settle” is permissive and does not expand the compulsory submission duty."],"citations":[{"quote":"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.","unit_id":"u4"},{"quote":"Starting 3